HST Office: Slides/Draw and shape dialogs laid out by the dialog layout rulebook.

Layout only (margins, spacing, alignment, column placement, character widths); no widget, id, label, string,
handler, mnemonic or accessibility change. Values from hst::design::layout:
- tab pages get a 12 px outer margin (the tabbed dialog shells keep 6), dialogs without tabs a 12 px border;
- groups 12 apart, two group columns 24 apart, rows of bordered controls 6 apart;
- labels of a block share one start-aligned column and are centred on their control's row;
- spin buttons of one column share one width (width-chars) instead of stretching over the dialog;
- Slide Show Settings puts Range under Mode next to Options, then the display group and Remote control across the
  dialog, so it fits a 1366x768 screen (it was 691 px tall on gtk3) with an unchanged focus order; the two Range
  list boxes get a 160 px minimum width (VCL list boxes take no width-chars);
- Position and Size, Line, Shadow, Duplicate, Insert Table, Bullets and Numbering, Interaction and Fontwork pages:
  the same columns and gaps on every tab, so switching tabs does not move the controls.
- Accessibility: Slide Show Settings' "Buttons size" label names its list box (label-for / labelled-by), and
  the Numbering page's "Start with" spin box takes the keyboard focus and is named by its check box, so its
  no-labelled-by suppression in sdraw.suppr goes.
Checked by tests/unit/test_ui_layout_rulebook.py (static) and tests/runtime/hst_dialog_layout_check.py (on screen,
cases of this group in tests/runtime/data/dialog-layout-c.json).

